Algorithm1 edge interpretation is explicit: when no later surviving copy meets the threshold, the scan stops and keeps all remaining copies; it does not delete or skip births. This conservative treatment must remain visible in any implementation-equivalence claim. No cap20 is silently inserted. The norm-smoothness sufficient beta derives from coordinatewise nonnegative frequencies plus Minkowski, and it is conservative; there is no claim that497 copies are necessary for all correct methods.

Combined decision from B006–B008: the compact native heuristic and an accuracy-linked reference solve different documented query contracts. Nearest-start counterexamples do not refute paper Algorithm1. A more accurate suffix estimator alone does not fix retention/query mismatch. The sufficient guarantee-preserving setting here nearly stores all starts, despite the small alphabet; the exact single-W baseline is strong. Do not tune a threshold until a matched error/space contract is stated, and do not expand native heuristic benchmarks as theorem validation.

